  },
  "typos": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "No typos found in instruction.md, task.toml, or the test/verifier scripts. 'eeever so slightly' in the task title looks unusual but was confirmed to be a verbatim copy of the real upstream GitHub issue title (#4978), not an authoring typo."
  },
  "tests_or_solution_in_image": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The Dockerfile only COPYs assets/ (screenshot) into the image after removing assets/bugs/; it explicitly states 'tests/ and solution/ are intentionally NOT copied into the image' and they are supplied at verify time via bind mounts, per test.sh applying /tests/test.patch and solve.sh applying /solution/fix.patch from outside the image."
  },
  "test_deps_in_image": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "pytest is deliberately excluded from the Dockerfile's pip install list (with a comment confirming this) and is instead installed inside tests/test.sh at verify time, keeping the agent-facing image free of test-only tooling."
  },
  "hardcoded_solution": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "solve.sh applies solution/fix.patch via git apply/patch, which makes the actual multi-hunk source-code edits (label rect repositioning, text template swap, temperament index swap, relations comparison operator, theme object id change) rather than printing or echoing a final answer. This was cross-checked against the real upstream fix commit (1edd03aa0) and matches it for the genuine bug plus the two additional synthetic-defect reversions."
